          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#general_definition"} General definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#further_discussion"} Further discussion
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Horizontal categorification
            or
            %em oidification
            (to be contrasted with the more famous
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} vertical categorification
            which is usually just called
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a concept is realized to be equivalent to a certain type of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magmoid"} magmoid
                with a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em
                    single
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %li
              %p and then this concept is generalized – or oidified – by passing to instances of such types of categories with more than one object.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #Groupoids.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (groups to groupoids)
              %br/
              The horizontal categorification of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
              are
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
              in which every morphism is invertible.
          %p
            Similar comments as the following Remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AreGroupoidsGeneralizedGroups"}
            apply generally to oidification:
          %p
          #AreGroupoidsGeneralizedGroups.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Groupoids"}
              there is an “inclusion”
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
              of (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoids"} delooping groupoids
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}(-)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Grp
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mi Grpd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    Grp &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Grpd
                    \\\
                    G &amp;\mapsto&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              Beware, though, that this 2-functor is
              %em not
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+fully+faithful+2-functor"} fully faithful
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi H
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G, H \in Grpd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-groupoid"} hom-groupoid
              between their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoids"} delooping groupoids
              is not quite the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to H
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              of that by the pointwise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint action
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⫽
                      %mi ad
                    %mi H
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Grpd\big(
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    ,\,
                    \\mathbf{B}H
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Grp\big(
                    G
                    ,\,
                    H
                    \\big)
                    \\sslash_{ad}
                    H
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              For instance, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = A
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Grp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Grpd\big(
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    ,\,
                    \\mathbf{B}A
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Grp\big(
                    G
                    ,\,
                    A
                    \\big)
                    \\times
                    \\mathbf{B}A
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              This is one formal way of seeing that it is not
              %em quite
              right to say that “groupoids are generalized groups”, not without further qualification:
            %p
              Namely, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              is canonically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
              (uniquely pointed by its single
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              = succeed "-construction" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd^\ast
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
              groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Grp
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Grpd
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    Grp &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Grpd^\ast
                    \\\
                    G &amp;\mapsto&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              and as such this
              %em is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+fully+faithful+2-functor"} fully faithful
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+2-categories"} equivalently
              identifying groups with
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+connected+groupoids"} pointed connected groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Grpd^\ast\big(
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    ,\,
                    \\mathbf{B}H
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Hom\big(
                    G
                    ,\,
                    H
                    \\big)
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              This is part of a general phenomenon discussed further at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
              (cf. also at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/May+recognition+theorem"} May recognition theorem
            %p
              In practice, for instance
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+groupoids"} Picard groupoids
              appear as generalized
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+2-groups"} abelian 2-groups
              and as such are in particular pointed (by their
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
          %p
          #Algebroids.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (algebras to algebroids)
              %br/
              A horizontal categorification of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras"} algebras
              are
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebroids"} algebroids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} categories enriched
              in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+vector+spaces"} category of vector spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              via the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (rings to ringoids)
              %br/
              A horizontal categorification of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
              are
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringoids"} ringoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} categories enriched
              over the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+abelian+groups"} category of abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              (cf.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2006/09/ringoids.html"} blog
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                \-algebras to
                = succeed "-categories)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %br/
              A horizontal categorification of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebras"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi \
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\*
                \-algebras
              hence ought to be known as
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                –algebroids
              but is usually known as
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star-category"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                    \-categories
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (spaces to spaceoids)
              %br/
              Since, by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand-Naimark+theorem"} Gelfand-Naimark theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
                \-algebras
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} dual
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Bertozzini"} Paolo Bertozzini
              et. al proposed to define
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaceoids"} spaceoids
              to be the entities
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formally dual
              to
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/01/spaceoids.html"} blog
          %p
          #Monoidoid.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (monoids to categories)
              %br/
              And an
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong exception to the rule
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
              are
              %em not
              called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidoids"} monoidoids
              – but are called…
              = succeed "!" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %p
              On the other hand, in the case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enrichment
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R+Mod"} R Mod
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              and the oidificies
              = succeed "-categories" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebroid"} algebroid
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Algebroids"}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (monads to bicategory-enriched categories)
              %br/
              A horizontal categorification of the notion of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
              is that of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+enriched+in+a+bicategory"} categories enriched in a bicategory
          %p
          #LawvereTheoriesAndOperads.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Lawvere theories and operads)
              %br/
              A horizontal categorification of a single-sorted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              are multisorted Lawvere theory. Analogously
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operads"} operads
              categorify to a many-colored operad.
          %p
          #InTypeTheory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              In
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+language+theory"} programming language theory
              = succeed ":" do
                %em introducing a type distinction
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lambda+calculus"} lambda calculus
              has models in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theories"} Lawvere theories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typed+lambda+calculus"} typed lambda calculus
              has models in Cartesian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
