          %h2#general_definition General definition
          %p
            Tom Leinster’s book “Higher Operads, Higher Categories” contains a general theory of horizontal categorification of a notion of algebraic structure, as long as the algebraic structure can be defined as the category of algebras for an operad. Leinster proves that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a (non-symmetric) operad in the category of sets, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            can be extended to an “fc-multicategory”
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma P
            %em suspension
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            satisfying certain co/completeness assumptions. For example, one can take
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}= \mathbf{Cat}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            whose algebras are monoidal categories has for its suspension (i.e., its horizontal categorification) the generalized operad whose algebras are precisely bicategories.
